  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, 72-hour customer notice, and prior-year reconciliation. S2 keeps the 55°C/5% test but avoids an automatic market ban and gives per-model results to customers/regulators without public publication. S3 sets a 6-year retrofit with alternative mitigation; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k threshold but recall is regulator-discretionary with open corrective action and prompt notice."
